{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531447-v20-maeghar-embrace-and-clan-disciplines","id":1531447,"title":"V20 Maeghar Embrace and Clan Disciplines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-24T17:56:36-08:00","id":1531447,"title":"V20 Maeghar Embrace and Clan Disciplines","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Three main questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>How does the Maeghar Disciplines get assigned?*</b></li> <li><b>What are the available Necromancy Paths for Maeghar and Kiasyd?</b> (the option in Lore of the Bloodlines that states Kiasyd can start with Necromancy instead of Dominate)</li> <li><b>IF a Maeghar appears only when a Vampire embraces a fae-blooded human, does the Sire Clan treat it as a regular clan member until abnormalities are discovered?</b> For example a Tremere embraces someone that happens to be fae-blooded, if it is not too abnormal, will it believe them to be Tremere and bring them into the Chantry, make them work on arcane research, etc, etc?</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">*The Maeghar write-up has:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Embrace: </b>A Maeghar herself rarely Embraces. She feels<br /> little need for companionship, so why should she curse another<br /> with her existence? If she does Embrace, it\u2019s usually because the<br /> childe has a very specific skillset that suits her purposes. When<br /> that purpose is met, the childe is either destroyed or set free.<br /> There is no consistency to which childer are killed and which<br /> released, as some Maeghar might see freedom as a reward for<br /> good services, whilst others view blessed death as such. <u>To<br /> create another Maeghar, a sire must embrace a fae-blooded<br /> mortal. If she does not, the resulting childe is always a Caitiff,<br /> since he lacks the unique spark to become a Maeghar.</u><br /> <br /> <b>Clan Disciplines:</b> Mytherceria or Necromancy (player\u2019s<br /> choice), plus <u>two others from sire\u2019s Clan Disciplines.</u> </div> </div> </div>Underline mine for emphasis.<br /> <br /> Does it mean that ANY regular vampire can produce a Maeghar? Otherwise how can a new Maeghar get the sire's &quot;Clan Disciplines&quot;?<br /> <br /> If what I am saying is right, what is the difference between Kiasyd and Maeghar? I seem to remember that fae-blooded human gets embraced, then you get a Kiasyd.<br /> </div> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-24-2024, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T07:29:21-08:00","id":1531469,"title":"","content":"1) Take the parent Clan. Pick one Discipline from that Clan's native Disciplines and exchange it for Necromancy or Mytherceria. Then keep the other two. Those are the Maeghar's three Favored Disciplines.<br /> <br /> 2) It's unknown. Likely they would have the physical ones since the Wraith-focused Paths didn't really get created until the Giovanni were Embraced, though given the weirdness of the Maeghar maybe one of them could have had something comparable.<br /> <br /> 3) from what I can recall, the sire realizes pretty quickly that the vampire came out &quot;wrong.&quot; Traditionally, sires would put down or abandon the Maeghar, but there could be the rare exception.<br /> <br /> Yes, any vampire can have a Maeghar spawn. Whenever a vampire (from any clan) embraces a mortal, if the mortal is fey blooded, there's a chance the childe could end up as a Maeghar instead of their sire's clan.<br /> <br /> The Kiasyd are essentially a Maeghar bloodline with a unique appearance and clan flaw. Whenever a Maeghar embraces, if the mortal was fey blooded, they turn into another Maeghar. If they weren't, then they're a Caitiff. We don't know exactly how the Kaisyd work, if they require their childe to be fey blooded, or if they can embrace anyone into the clan like any other vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T08:03:29-08:00","id":1531470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531447-v20-maeghar-embrace-and-clan-disciplines?p=1531469#post1531469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kiasyd are essentially a Maeghar bloodline with a unique appearance and clan flaw. Whenever a Maeghar embraces, if the mortal was fey blooded, they turn into another Maeghar. If they weren't, then they're a Caitiff. We don't know exactly how the Kaisyd work, if they require their childe to be fey blooded, or if they can embrace anyone into the clan like any other vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I understood it is that (current) Kiasyd are a 'proper' bloodline and direct descendants of Marconius after he messed around with fey blood, and a Kiasyd Embrace results in another Kiasyd, regardless of whether the childe has fey blood or not. The Maeghar used to be called Kiasyd until Marconius claimed that moniker for his bloodline, but the only commonality between the two is the involvement of fey blood and by extension Mytheratica. The whole thing is imo just fluff that was made to retcon things in line between editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T15:25:43-08:00","id":1531704,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> Thanks for your time and answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}